# False positives: PEM header/footer MARKER STRINGS, not key material.
#
# The connector implements a _normalize_pem() helper that reflows a pasted
# cert/key block to strict 64-column PEM. To do that it has to know the
# header/footer delimiters, so it carries a literal list of them (block_types).
# gitleaks' private-key rule is a literal string match with no code-semantics
# awareness, so it fires on the delimiters themselves. No actual key bytes are
# present anywhere in this package: verified by reading the surrounding function
# (it is a tuple list of delimiter constants) and by scanning the whole export
# for base64 runs longer than 60 chars (zero hits).
#
# Same pattern as cyberark_ccp's _normalize_pem() in the UC1 handover.
#
# NOTE: these fingerprints are line-pinned AND path-pinned, and they have drifted
# on every connector change: 402 -> 490-492 (v1.0.6) -> 582-584 (v1.0.1) ->
# 570-572 (v1.0.2, after _apply_client_limit and its call sites were removed) ->
# 564-566 (2026-08-31, below). Re-check on every export, or the gate will miss a
# real finding or fail the commit.
#
# 2026-08-31 — repinned for the SDK removal, and this time the PATHS moved too,
# not just the line numbers:
#   * The SDK app was deleted, so its three connectors/source/efficientip_ddi/
